        "discovery_date": "2025-09-02T13:03:56.452000+00:00",
        "ids": [
          {
            "system_name": "Red Hat Bugzilla ID",
            "text": "2392605"
          }
        ],
        "notes": [
          {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in libxstl/libxml2. The 'exsltDynMapFunction' function in libexslt/dynamic.c does not contain a recursion depth check, which may cause an infinite loop via a specially crafted XSLT document while handling 'dyn:map()', leading to stack exhaustion and a local denial of service.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "libxslt: libxml2: Inifinite recursion at exsltDynMapFunction function in libexslt/dynamic.c",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "No evidence was found for arbitrary memory corruption through this flaw, limiting its impact to Availability only, and reducing its severity to Moderate.",
